---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Think — Greg O'Brien" description="Notes on agentic AI, product management, and applied philosophy — quick, practical pieces from day-to-day thinking." current={2}>
<div data-screen-label="Notes archive">
<div data-hero="1" style="border-top:1px solid var(--edge);border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule);margin-top:38px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr">
<div data-hero-left="1" style="padding:96px 56px 84px;border-right:1px solid var(--rule)">
<div style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)">Think</div>
<h1 style="margin:18px 0 0;font-family:Newsreader,serif;font-weight:400;font-size:54px;line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.02em">Notes, in <span style="font-style:italic">full</span>.</h1>
</div>
<div data-hero-right="1" style="padding:calc(96px + 32.5px) 56px 84px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px">
<p style="margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;max-width:46ch;color:var(--body)">I write to learn, and I enjoy distilling an idea into something short and clear. These are quick, practical pieces from my day-to-day thinking. Shorter, half-formed thoughts live in the Stream.</p>
<div style="display:flex;gap:18px;font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--muted)"><span>3 notes</span><span>·</span><a href="/stream" style="color:var(--accent);text-decoration:none" class="h-ul">Stream</a></div>
</div>
</div>
<div style="padding:40px 56px 14px;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline">
<span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)">2026</span>
<a href="/" style="font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none;transition:color .2s ease" class="h-ink">Home →</a>
</div>
<div style="padding:14px 56px 44px">
<a href="/think/jev-and-the-case-for-a-model-that-doesnt-talk" data-note-row="1" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:220px 1fr;gap:24px;align-items:start;padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ruleSoft);text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);transition:color .2s ease" class="h-accent">
<div style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9;border:1px solid var(--edge);padding:14px;position:relative;overflow:hidden;background:#68c8f0"><img src="/images/think/jev-hero.webp" alt="A fountain pen whose nib has drawn a single small tick on an otherwise empty page" width="1344" height="768" loading="lazy" style="position:absolute;inset:0;width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;object-position:right center;display:block" /></div>
<div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:20px"><span style="font-family:Newsreader,serif;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3">Jev and the case for a model that doesn't talk</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap">23 Sep 2026</span></div>
<p style="margin:9px 0 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--body);max-width:52ch">Most of an agent's work is small judgement calls. TypeSafe has built a model for exactly that, and I think the idea is bigger than the product.</p>
</div>
</a>
<a href="/think/why-agent-is-doing-too-much-work-as-a-word" data-note-row="1" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:220px 1fr;gap:24px;align-items:start;padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--ruleSoft);text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);transition:color .2s ease" class="h-accent">
<div style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9;border:1px solid var(--edge);background:var(--stripe);display:flex;align-items:flex-end;padding:14px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap">[ AGENT PHOTO ]</span></div>
<div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:20px"><span style="font-family:Newsreader,serif;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3">Why "agent" is doing too much work as a word</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap">14 Aug 2026</span></div>
<p style="margin:9px 0 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--body);max-width:52ch">Half the industry means "chatbot," the other half means something closer to software with judgement. That gap is the whole story.</p>
</div>
</a>
<a href="/think/product-management-is-applied-philosophy" data-note-row="1" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:220px 1fr;gap:24px;align-items:start;padding:22px 0;text-decoration:none;color:var(--ink);transition:color .2s ease" class="h-accent">
<div style="aspect-ratio:16 / 9;border:1px solid var(--edge);background:var(--stripe);display:flex;align-items:flex-end;padding:14px"><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap">[ PM PHILOSOPHY PHOTO ]</span></div>
<div>
<div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:20px"><span style="font-family:Newsreader,serif;font-size:23px;line-height:1.3">Product management is applied philosophy</span><span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap">19 Jun 2026</span></div>
<p style="margin:9px 0 0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--body);max-width:52ch">Roadmaps are really just values written down and defended in public. The job is philosophy with a deadline.</p>
</div>
</a>
</div>
</div>
</Layout>
